 			<p>“Jo! Jo! where are you?” cried Meg, at the foot of the garret stairs.</p>
 			<p>“Here!” answered a husky voice from above; and, running up, Meg found her sister eating apples and crying over the <i epub:type="se:name.publication.book">Heir of Redclyffe</i>, wrapped up in a comforter on an old three-legged sofa by the sunny window. This was Jo’s favorite refuge; and here she loved to retire with half a dozen russets and a nice book, to enjoy the quiet and the society of a pet rat who lived near by, and didn’t mind her a particle. As Meg appeared, Scrabble whisked into his hole. Jo shook the tears off her cheeks, and waited to hear the news.</p>
